// =====================================================================
// Sentinel onboarding / telemetry coverage check
// =====================================================================
// Purpose : Given an authoritative list of expected hosts, determine which
//           are emitting telemetry into the workspace and which are not.
// Hosts   : 527 unique (normalized to short, lowercase hostname).
// Match   : short hostname across Heartbeat / Syslog / CommonSecurityLog /
//           DeviceInfo. Returns one row per device with Status + Feeds.
//
// CAVEAT - read before trusting the MISSING count:
//   ~85% of this list is network / infrastructure gear (switches, OOB cards,
//   SAN switches, 3PAR/XP storage, HSMs). These do NOT run the AMA agent;
//   they ship syslog/CEF and frequently log by MANAGEMENT IP, not a
//   resolvable hostname. Such devices can read as MISSING on a name join
//   even while shipping logs. For Status=="MISSING" rows matching
//   oob / sanswt / 3par / xp / hsm patterns, re-check against SourceIP /
//   DeviceAddress in Syslog / CommonSecurityLog before declaring a real gap.
//
//   FortiGate/SD-WAN: confirm which CEF field carries the name with
//     CommonSecurityLog | where DeviceVendor == "Fortinet"
//     | distinct DeviceName, SourceHostName
//   before relying on the DeviceName join.
// =====================================================================

let lookback = 24h;

// --- authoritative expected list (short lowercase hostnames) ---------
let expected = datatable(Computer:string)
